From 5f2eab464db2e93dac5aad6b004446c3052f195f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Branch <andrewbranch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:54:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Identify source files by node ID in request node handles

Location handles sent by the client repeated the file's full path
("index.kind.path"). Nodes decoded from a server-encoded source file now send
"index.kind.#nodeID", using the source-file node ID already carried in the
encoded file, and the server resolves it through a lazily built per-program
index. IDs of files encoded for a client but absent from the requested program
fall back to path lookup, preserving resolution of nodes from compatible
standalone files. getNodeId and compiler-produced handles keep the path form.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
